{
  "id": "Compound::DB00220 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Nelfinavir, a protease inhibitor, is shown to bind to Cyp2b6 and Cyp2c9, two cytochrome P450 enzymes, through multiple pathways. These binding interactions are supported by high-confidence scores, suggesting a potential role in modulating the activity of these enzymes. Cyp2b6 is involved in the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, while Cyp2c9 is associated with oxidoreductase activity, both of which are catalyzed by these enzymes. The shared participation in these activities by Cyp2c9 implies that Nelfinavir may influence the metabolic processing of substrates that involve these enzymatic functions. The integrated evidence suggests that Nelfinavir could modulate Cyp2c9 activity through direct binding, potentially affecting the metabolism of substrates that are oxidized or reduced by this enzyme. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple pathways linking Nelfinavir to Cyp2c9, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
